<control>{"schema":"stage-control-v1","digest":"Current official stdio specification reserves stdout for valid MCP messages and permits UTF-8 diagnostic logging on stderr.","questionId":"rq-003","question":"What does the current MCP stdio specification permit or prohibit servers from writing to stdout and stderr?","covers":["Server stdout and stderr rules"],"extractedFacts":[{"slotId":"slot-004","slotLabel":"Server stdout permitted content and prohibitions","entity":"Model Context Protocol stdio server","value":"The server writes JSON-RPC messages to stdout; each message is a single request, notification, or response. It MUST NOT write anything to stdout that is not a valid MCP message.","factType":"policy","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"],"sourceRefs":["wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83"],"sourceTitleOrPublisher":"Model Context Protocol specification — stdio","sourceQuality":"primary","confidence":"high","quote":"The server **MUST NOT** write anything to its `stdout` that is not a valid MCP\n  message.","notes":"Plain-text logs, banners, and debug prints are therefore prohibited on stdout; this is an application of the normative rule."},{"slotId":"slot-005","slotLabel":"Server stderr logging permissions and normative strength","entity":"Model Context Protocol stdio server","value":"The server MAY write UTF-8 strings to stderr for any logging purposes, including informational, debug, and error messages.","factType":"policy","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"],"sourceRefs":["wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83"],"sourceTitleOrPublisher":"Model Context Protocol specification — stdio","sourceQuality":"primary","confidence":"high","quote":"The server **MAY** write UTF-8 strings to `stderr` for any logging purposes\n  including informational, debug, and error messages.","notes":"MAY is permission, not a requirement to log. Stderr is not restricted to errors."},{"slotId":"slot-005","slotLabel":"Server stderr logging permissions and normative strength","entity":"Model Context Protocol stdio client handling server stderr","value":"The client MAY capture, forward, or ignore server stderr and SHOULD NOT assume stderr output indicates error conditions.","factType":"policy","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"],"sourceRefs":["wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83"],"sourceTitleOrPublisher":"Model Context Protocol specification — stdio","sourceQuality":"primary","confidence":"high","quote":"The client **MAY** capture, forward, or ignore the server's `stderr` output and\n  **SHOULD NOT** assume `stderr` output indicates error conditions.","notes":"Client-side context prevents interpreting all server stderr output as failure."}],"claims":[{"claim":"Server stdout MUST NOT contain anything that is not a valid MCP message.","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"],"sourceRefs":["wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83"],"sourceTitleOrPublisher":"Official MCP stdio specification","dateOrYear":"2026-07-28","sourceQuality":"primary","scopeItems":["Server stdout and stderr rules"],"factSlotIds":["slot-004"]},{"claim":"Servers MAY write UTF-8 strings to stderr for informational, debug, and error logging.","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"],"sourceRefs":["wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83"],"sourceTitleOrPublisher":"Official MCP stdio specification","dateOrYear":"2026-07-28","sourceQuality":"primary","scopeItems":["Server stdout and stderr rules"],"factSlotIds":["slot-005"]},{"claim":"Clients MAY capture, forward, or ignore server stderr and SHOULD NOT assume it indicates errors.","sourceUrls":["https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md"],"sourceRefs":["wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83"],"sourceTitleOrPublisher":"Official MCP stdio specification","dateOrYear":"2026-07-28","sourceQuality":"primary","scopeItems":["Server stdout and stderr rules"],"factSlotIds":["slot-005"]}],"additionalUnverifiedLeads":[],"sources":[{"sourceRef":"wsrc_ff966eae34ec1ec6ab48a4f0cf055b83","sourceUrl":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md","title":"Official MCP specification — stdio","quote":"The server **MUST NOT** write anything to its `stdout` that is not a valid MCP\n  message.","matchType":"exact"},{"sourceRef":"wsrc_6f2e06f5a0dd2c8d98ce75ab416660e7","sourceUrl":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/versioning","title":"Official MCP versioning","quote":"The **current** protocol version is [**2026-07-28**](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28.md).","matchType":"exact"},{"sourceRef":"wsrc_3af3257c452fc577322dd1fe372b693b","sourceUrl":"https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/latest/basic/transports","title":"Official MCP transport overview","quote":"[stdio](https://modelcontextprotocol.io/specification/2026-07-28/basic/transports/stdio.md): newline-delimited\n   messages over the standard streams of a client-launched subprocess.","matchType":"exact"}],"caveats":["The requested local schema could not be inspected because this public-web task prohibits filesystem reads; no schema-validation tool is enabled."],"sourceQualityNotes":["Official versioning explicitly identifies 2026-07-28 as current, and the latest transport URL resolves to that version. Currency is based on retrieved official navigation rather than remembered release dates.","Search results mostly returned SDK documentation; normative evidence was instead retrieved from known official specification entry URLs and their linked stdio binding."],"budgetLedger":{"searchBudget":3,"searchCallsUsed":2,"searchQueriesAttempted":["site:modelcontextprotocol.io specification stdio server stdout stderr MUST","site:modelcontextprotocol.io/specification \"The server MUST NOT\" \"stdout\"","site:modelcontextprotocol.io/specification \"2025-11-25\" transports"],"omittedSearchQueries":[],"budgetExhausted":false,"gapRecorded":false}}</control>
<analysis>The current official versioning page identifies version 2026-07-28. Its stdio binding supplies direct, exact evidence for both required slots.

Preserve the distinction between obligation and permission: stdout MUST contain only valid MCP messages; stderr MAY carry UTF-8 logging text, including non-error diagnostics. The specification does not require servers to log, nor does it restrict stderr to errors. Its companion client rule explicitly permits ignoring stderr and says clients SHOULD NOT assume it indicates error conditions.

Plain-text stdout logs violate the valid-message restriction; that example is an inference from the explicit normative prohibition, not separately quoted specification wording.</analysis>
